sylvie: heads-up: support saw crashes after we switched to invokeEnvelope. Their parser expected tool_call and args as an object.
jamie: can you paste the minimal failing payload?
sylvie: from support:
{
  "invokeEnvelope": {
    "tool": "search",
    "arguments": "{\"q\":\"pricing api\"}"
  }
}
marco: classic double-encoded arguments. Plan: add a short H3 'Compatibility adapters' to /docs/guides/structured-output.md with tiny defensive snippets (py/ts/go) and a one-line migration note.
tasha: CI checklist: run docs build + link-checker before merge. ci-bot: link-checker will run on PR.
jamie: python defensive snippet I'll add:
```py
import json
def parse_args(env):
    a = env.get('arguments')
    if isinstance(a, str):
        try:
            return json.loads(a)
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            return {}
    return a or {}
```
marco: TS equivalent in PR:
```ts
export function normalizeEnvelope(resp:any){
  const env = resp.invokeEnvelope ?? resp.tool_call ?? resp;
  let args = env?.arguments;
  if(typeof args === 'string'){
    try{ args = JSON.parse(args); }catch{ args = {}; }
  }
  return {...env, arguments: args};
}
```
sylvie: include a one-line unit test example and call out not to use regex extraction. Recommend JSON Schema validation then a small adapter.
tasha: editorial: pick consistent term (we use 'invokeEnvelope') and add anchor H3 'Compatibility adapters'. I'll do final pass after link-check.
marco: opened draft PR with snippets and anchor, tagging eng-ml for guidance. ci-bot: PR created (checks pending).
